# Rationale: Benchmark content parity: B1 chunks carry description + lifecycle status; parity verified by containment

Commit 29cac60c28 changes both the chunk schema and the parity check. The original constraint stated "each chunk's body text matches the graph's hasDescription for that record" (exact equality). The new implementation intentionally makes chunks richer — `text = "# {title}

Lifecycle status: {status}

{desc}"` — to give B1 the same currency signal B2 carries. Exact equality fails because the chunk prepends title and status lines. Parity is now verified by hasDescription *containment* in chunk text. Additionally the SPARQL title join switched from STRENDS(hasTitle) to rdfs:label (to include SystemComponents). These changes invalidate the original constraint's implementation description.
